<p class="ih-label">How we own</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ih-h2"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ih-h2">We buy companies<br>to keep them.</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ih-p"} -->
<p class="ih-p">Ishizue buys companies in order to keep them. The holding company is privately held. The Ishizue Foundation owns the majority, and colleagues have held shares through the employee share plan since 2003. Money the companies earn stays available to them first. Reports are published because the board chooses to publish them, year after year, from the office in Rotterdam.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ih-p"} -->
<p class="ih-p">Local management stays in place, and the name on the door stays too. A company that joins is still that company. Ishizue Materials, Northquay Logistics, Lindholm Precision, Verda Facilities, Calder Food Partners and Ishizue Renewables continue from Rotterdam, Antwerp, Gothenburg, Utrecht, Hamburg and Aarhus. The holding office at Maaskade 41 employs 58 people. Its work is ownership, governance and a shared back office, while the yards, warehouses, workshops and sites carry on under the people who know them.</p>
